# Payverge backend environment
#
# Docker Compose is the supported deployment path. Use the canonical root
# template instead of maintaining backend-only values here:
#
#   cd ..
#   cp .env.example .env
#   docker compose --env-file .env config
#
# For one-off local `go run ./cmd/app` work, export the backend variables from
# ../.env or pass the same values as CLI flags. See ../README.md for the env
# matrix, and ../docs/ONBOARDING.md for the
# "root .env is canonical, per-service stubs are dead" orientation.
#
# Sentry backend variables are listed in ../.env.example:
# SENTRY_DSN
# SENTRY_ENVIRONMENT
# SENTRY_RELEASE
# SENTRY_ENABLED
# SENTRY_ENABLE_LOGS
# SENTRY_ENABLE_TRACING
# SENTRY_TRACES_SAMPLE_RATE
# SENTRY_LOG_LEVELS
